<SiteHeader page="corporate.html" current="corporate.html" />

<section class="page-hero">
<div class="wrap">
<p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Corporate</p>
<p class="eyebrow on-dark">Corporate &amp; Concierge</p>
<h1 class="display">For executive assistants and travel teams.</h1>
<div class="rule"></div>
<p class="lead">One accountable account for recurring executive travel across South Florida — consolidated billing, saved preferences, and a direct line that picks up. The point of contact who confirms the booking is the one accountable for it.</p>
<div class="page-actions">
<a class="btn btn-light" href="tel:+17869316699">Call now</a>
<a class="btn btn-light" href="https://wa.me/17869316699?text=Hi%2C%20I%27d%20like%20to%20open%20a%20corporate%20account." target="_blank" rel="noopener">WhatsApp</a>
<a class="btn btn-ghost" href="contact.html#book">Open an account</a>
</div>
<p class="trust-line">+1 786 931 ONYX (6699) · Licensed &amp; insured · Miami-Dade Permit #64666 · D-U-N-S&reg; 13-860-0693</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section-soft">
<div class="wrap split">
<div class="prose reveal">
<h2 class="h2">Less to manage, fewer surprises.</h2>
<div class="rule"></div>
<p>Recurring travel shouldn't mean re-explaining preferences every time or chasing a dispatcher. With an Onyx account, your executives' preferences are on file, billing is consolidated, and changes go to one person who answers — not a queue.</p>
<p>Certificate of insurance is available on request, which matters when your office or a venue requires it before a booking clears.</p>
</div>
<div class="figure reveal">
<div class="kicker">One<br>account.<br><em>One contact.</em></div>
<p>Airport runs, client dinners, roadshows, and full-day coverage — billed together, handled by the same accountable partner.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section-dark">
<div class="wrap split center">
<div class="prose reveal">
<p class="eyebrow on-dark">Account features</p>
<h2 class="h2">What an account includes.</h2>
<div class="rule"></div>
<ul class="points">
<li><i class="mark"></i><span><b>Consolidated billing.</b> One statement, clean records for expense reporting.</span></li>
<li><i class="mark"></i><span><b>Authorized bookers.</b> Executive assistants and travel coordinators can book and confirm rides directly on the account, without going through the traveler.</span></li>
<li><i class="mark"></i><span><b>Ride confirmations.</b> Each booking is confirmed back in writing — vehicle, time, and pickup point — before the day of travel.</span></li>
<li><i class="mark"></i><span><b>Saved preferences.</b> Greeting, route, temperature, water, charging — on file per traveler.</span></li>
<li><i class="mark"></i><span><b>Cost centers.</b> Trips can be tagged by department or project for internal billing, on request.</span></li>
<li><i class="mark"></i><span><b>Direct line.</b> Reach the person responsible, not a call center.</span></li>
<li><i class="mark"></i><span><b>COI &amp; W-9 on request.</b> Provided when your office, venue, or procurement process requires it.</span></li>
<li><i class="mark"></i><span><b>Discretion.</b> Unmarked vehicle, no detail repeated outside the booking.</span></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="feat-img reveal"><picture><source type="image/avif" srcset="interior-seats.avif" /><img src="interior-seats.webp" alt="Black leather second-row captain's seats inside the Onyx Executive Miami Suburban" width="700" height="933" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" /></picture></div>
</div>
</section>
